.he "alarm (2)                    4/6/83                     alarm (2)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
alarm
- set the alarm clock
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd
alarm(seconds)
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
This call sets the "alarm clock", which will send an
alarm signal to the calling process after the given
number of seconds (see signal (2)).  Meanwhile, the
process continues to run.

An argument of 0 turns the alarm clock off.

See also pause (2) and sleep (2).
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
If an alarm was previously set but not yet triggered,
alarm returns the number of seconds remaining until the
old alarm.  Otherwise it returns 0.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ASSEMBLER
.in +5
.br
.bd
(alarm = 27)
.br
.bd
(seconds in hl)
.br
.bd
sys; alarm
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
The time remaining on any old alarm is returned in hl.
There is no error return.
